# emergent.feedback — Playwright E2E configuration
#
# Copy to `e2e/.env` (git-ignored) and adjust. Every value has a safe default,
# so the deterministic `own` + `host` suites run with zero configuration.
#
# ── Local server (own pages) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The test server is launched by playwright.config.ts. The JWT secret below MUST
# match it so the suite can mint session tokens offline (no GitHub round-trip).
E2E_JWT_SECRET=e2e-secret
E2E_API_PORT=18095
E2E_FIXTURE_PORT=18096
# Parallelism. Default 1: the test server uses SQLite and concurrent feedback
# writes can 500. Raise only against a Postgres-backed server.
E2E_WORKERS=1

# MCP endpoint auth. Must match the server's MCP_API_KEY.
E2E_MCP_API_KEY=e2e-mcp-key

# Identity encoded into minted test tokens.
E2E_USER=e2e-user
E2E_AVATAR=

# Default repo used in feedback payloads.
E2E_REPO=e2e/demo

# ── Remote host app (optional, env-gated) ───────────────────────────────────
# When E2E_HOST_URL is set, the `remote` project runs against a deployed page
# that already embeds the emergent.feedback script.
# E2E_HOST_URL=https://app.example.com/dashboard
#
# Path to a Playwright storageState JSON (cookies + localStorage) for the host
# app's own login. Relative paths resolve against the e2e/ directory.
#   npm run login     # drives a hosted OIDC login (Zitadel, Auth0, ...)
#   npx playwright codegen --save-storage=e2e/.auth/host.json https://app.example.com
# The credentials below are read by `npm run login` (E2E_TEST_USER_* take
# precedence) and by the `remote-auth` setup project, a fallback for hosts that
# serve a plain email/password form themselves.
# E2E_STORAGE_STATE=.auth/host.json
# E2E_TEST_USER_EMAIL=
# E2E_TEST_USER_PASSWORD=
# E2E_HOST_USER=
# E2E_HOST_PASS=
#
# Guard: remote specs only submit feedback (write) when this is truthy.
# E2E_ALLOW_WRITES=
